  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the operator, I want a **Réglages › Expérimental** section where each modern option I keep refining sits behind a switch that is off by default, so that the M4 build keeps the legacy behaviour (ezzz's 1:1 non-regression) while no code of the new composer, the 5-item tab bar, the MP storage switches or the current topic rows is lost. (Operator, 2026-11-14, after ezzz's comments of 2026-11-14 on #425, #817, #825, #855, #753, #822, #859 and #896.)\n\n### Why this comes first (ordering)\n\nThis issue **must merge before** #855 (full-screen composer), #817 (topic rows), #859 (MP storage switches) and the #853 / #895 composer work. Otherwise #855 would replace the modern composer instead of adding the legacy path next to it. Each of them carries `### Blocked by` #903.\n\n### Scope\n\n1. **Section Réglages › Expérimental**, at the end of the Réglages list, with one footer sentence: \"Options en cours de mise au point, désactivées par défaut.\" It is organised in **sub-menus by theme** (operator, 2026-11-14), for example Composer, Listes, Messages, Chargement des images. Each row is a switch or a picker, with an ⓘ that explains what it changes.\n2. **One entry point in the code**:\n   - an `ExperimentalFeature` enum (one case per option) and an `ExperimentalSettings` store with one device-level key per option, all default `false`;\n   - the new keys are added to the ADR 0013 storage matrix (Device-only);\n   - views and models read a flag through that store, never a raw `UserDefaults` key.\n3. **Code isolation**:\n   - each option's code moves to `App/SwiftHFR/Experimental/<Option>/`;\n   - every place where an option replaces, wraps or disables code carries one marker comment, `// EXPERIMENTAL(<option>, #<issue>): replaces <view or behaviour>`, so `git grep \"EXPERIMENTAL(\"` lists them all;\n   - removing an option means deleting its folder, its enum case and its markers.\n4. **Options at the start** (the modern code moves behind its switch in this PR; nothing is rewritten):\n\n| Option (enum case) | Switch label | On (experimental) | Off (default) | Issue |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `modernComposer` | Composer moderne | today's compact composer card (#888) and its follow-ups #853 and #895 | the legacy full-screen composer, delivered by #855. **Until #855 merges, this PR keeps the switch ON by default** so the app is never left without a composer; #855 flips the default to off. | #904 |\n| `searchTab` | Recherche dans la barre | a 5-item tab bar with Recherche left of Plus | the 4-item legacy bar | #896 |\n| `mpStorageSwitches` | Stockage MP détaillé | the per-function switches of Stockage MP: Liste noire partagée, Favoris de messages, MP multiples → dark topic | the single legacy switch \"Activer le stockage MP\" | #859 |\n| `flagIconRows` | Lignes avec icônes de drapeau | today's topic rows: unread dot and flag icons in front of the title | the legacy rows of #817: whole-row tint by flag type, no icon before the title | #905 |\n| `imageLoadingChoice` | Chargement des images (sub-menu) | the Jamais / Wi-Fi uniquement / Toujours picker | always load, as legacy | #902 |\n\n   `searchTab`, the #859 switches and `imageLoadingChoice` are not built yet: this PR only adds their enum cases and rows, hidden until their PR lands (no dead switch).\n5. **Offline save disabled, not experimental** (#822):\n   - hide the \"save this page offline\" entry and every offline button or menu item;\n   - keep the code, marked `// DISABLED(offline, #822): kept for a later design (#846), not reachable`;\n   - no setting for it.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Réglages › Expérimental lists the switches of the shipped options, each with an ⓘ; VoiceOver reads its explanation.\n- [ ] `git grep \"EXPERIMENTAL(\"` lists every replaced place, and each option's code is under `App/SwiftHFR/Experimental/<Option>/`.\n- [ ] Tests cover both paths of each shipped option (switch on, switch off), and a test checks that no offline entry is reachable.\n- [ ] The modern composer behaves exactly as before with its switch on (#888's hosted layout tests unchanged and green).\n- [ ] ADR 0013 lists the new device keys.\n- [ ] GAP rows are updated through the PR's `### Ledger` section (offline: removed; composer: legacy by default).\n\n### Routing\n\n`host: mac` (it moves the composer that mac/M1 is reworking in #853, so one session owns both). Opus authors, Fable reviews.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
